# Engineering defaults

- Prefer small, reviewable diffs. Do not expand scope beyond the request.
- Match existing naming, layout, and patterns before inventing new ones.
- Read surrounding code and docs before changing behavior or inventing APIs.
- Never commit secrets (API keys, tokens, credentials). Keep them in local `.env` (gitignored); commit only `.env.example` placeholders.
- Do not update git config, force-push shared branches, or skip hooks unless explicitly asked.
- Only create commits / PRs when the user asks.
- Avoid editing markdown/docs the user did not ask for, unless required for the change to be usable.
- Prefer fixing root causes over speculative refactors or drive-by cleanups.
